04 — Navidrome Setup

What is this for?
Navidrome is a self-hosted music streaming server. It indexes your music library and lets you stream your music from anywhere using apps like Substreamer on your phone. It is accessed remotely via Tailscale when off the home network.

Prerequisites
Portainer is running on the Ubuntu Server VM
Your music files are stored somewhere accessible on the VM (e.g. /home/yourusername/music)

Creating the Music Folder
If you do not already have a music folder, create one:

   mkdir -p ~/music

Place your music files in this folder. Navidrome supports MP3, FLAC, AAC, OGG, and most common formats.

Deploying Navidrome in Portainer
Open Portainer at https://10.0.0.x:9443
Go to Stacks → Add Stack
Name it navidrome
Paste the following into the Web editor:

   version: "3"
   services:
     navidrome:
       image: deluan/navidrome:latest
       container_name: navidrome
       restart: unless-stopped
       ports:
         - "4533:4533"
       environment:
         ND_SCANSCHEDULE: 1h
         ND_LOGLEVEL: info
         ND_SESSIONTIMEOUT: 24h
         ND_BASEURL: ""
       volumes:
         - "/home/yourusername/navidrome/data:/data"
         - "/home/yourusername/music:/music:ro"

Replace yourusername with your actual Ubuntu username.
The :ro at the end of the music volume means read-only — Navidrome will never modify your files.

Click Deploy the stack

Accessing Navidrome
Open a browser and navigate to:

   http://10.0.0.x:4533

First Time Setup
Create an admin username and password when prompted
Navidrome will automatically scan your music folder
Wait for the scan to complete — you will see your library populate
Log in and verify your music library appears correctly

Connecting Substreamer on iPhone
Substreamer uses the Subsonic API that Navidrome supports natively.

Install Substreamer from the App Store
Open Substreamer and go to Settings → Add Server
Enter the following:
   Server URL    http://10.0.0.x:4533  (on home network)
                 http://100.x.x.x:4533 (via Tailscale when away from home)
   Username      your Navidrome admin username
   Password      your Navidrome admin password
Tap Test Connection to verify it works

Note: The Tailscale IP (100.x.x.x) is used when you are not on your home network. See the Tailscale setup doc for details.

